ured\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] Runbook created\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] Deployment runbook reviewed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review completed\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] Dependency licenses compatible\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] OWASP Top 10 checklist completed\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] Data handling compliant with requirements\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation complete (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| [Name] | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| [Name] | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| [Name] | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Each task names the verify command whose output proves it.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`, then `Verify:` with the command whose output proves the task.\n\nShell variables used below, set once by the implementer:\n- `S`: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit`\n- `SCRIPT`: `$S/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`\n- `P`: `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the script end to end and record its output surfaces (no file). Verify: `rg -n 'output_text|output_json|Recommended Level|JSON_OUTPUT' \"$SCRIPT\"` prints the two output functions, the level line and the JSON flag.\n- [ ] T002 Capture the pre-change output corpus (`scratch/baseline/`). Run eight invocations - `--loc 50 --files 2`, `--loc 200 --files 5 --api`, `--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural`, `--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --no-recommend-phases`, `--loc 100 --files 3 --json`, `--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --no-recommend-phases --json`, `--loc`, and no arguments - writing `<case>.out`, `<case>.err` and `<case>.code` for each. Verify: `ls \"$P/scratch/baseline/\"*.out | wc -l` prints `8`.\n- [ ] T003 Confirm the test harness runs (no file). Verify: `cd \"$S\" && npx vitest run runtime/cli/tests/create-unknown-options.vitest.ts --config vitest.config.ts` prints `Test Files 1 passed`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Write the failing regression test (`$S/runtime/cli/tests/recommend-level-quiet.vitest.ts`). Cover the quiet line, unchanged default output, JSON precedence, the error paths and `--help`. Verify: the focused run fails only on the `--quiet` assertions and passes the default-output assertion, proving the test observes the missing feature rather than a broken harness.\n- [ ] T005 Add `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` beside `JSON_OUTPUT` (`$SCRIPT`). Verify: `rg -n 'QUIET_OUTPUT=false' \"$SCRIPT\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T006 Add `format_level_line()` and call it from both `output_text()` and the new quiet path (`$SCRIPT`). Verify: `rg -n 'format_level_line' \"$SCRIPT\"` prints the definition and both call sites.\n- [ ] T007 Add `output_quiet()` that prints the shared level line and nothing else (`$SCRIPT`). Verify: `rg -n 'output_quiet' \"$SCRIPT\"` prints the definition.\n- [ ] T008 Add the `--quiet` case to the argument loop (`$SCRIPT`). Verify: `rg -n -A 3 -- '--quiet\\)' \"$SCRIPT\"` shows `QUIET_OUTPUT=true` and `shift`.\n- [ ] T009 Change the output dispatch to JSON, then quiet, then text (`$SCRIPT`). Verify: `rg -n -A 7 'JSON_OUTPUT\" = true' \"$SCRIPT\"` shows the three-branch order with JSON first.\n- [ ] T010 Add `--quiet` to the file header OPTIONS block (`$SCRIPT`). Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet' \"$SCRIPT\" | head -3` includes the header line above the `--json` line.\n- [ ] T011 Add `--quiet` and an example to `show_help()` (`$SCRIPT`). Verify: `bash \"$SCRIPT\" --help | rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints `2`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T012 Check shell syntax (no file). Verify: `bash -n \"$SCRIPT\"` exits 0 with no output.\n- [ ] T013 Check the quiet line shape (no file). Verify: `bash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet | wc -l` prints `1`, and `bash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet | od -c | head -2` shows `R e c o m m e n d e d` at offset 0 with no leading newline.\n- [ ] T014 Check the quiet line across the level range (no file). For `--loc 50 --files 2`, `--loc 200 --files 5 --api` and `--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural`, compare the quiet output with the second line of the default output. Verify: `for args in ...; do diff <(bash \"$SCRIPT\" $args | sed -n '2p') <(bash \"$SCRIPT\" $args --quiet); done` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T015 Check default output is byte-identical (no file). Verify: for each of the eight corpus cases, `diff -u \"$P/scratch/baseline/<case>.out\" <(bash \"$SCRIPT\" <args>)` and the same for `.err` print nothing, and each `.code` matches the observed exit status.\n- [ ] T016 Check JSON precedence (no file). Verify: `diff <(bash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 100 --files 3 --json) <(bash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 100 --files 3 --json --quiet)` prints nothing, and `bash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 100 --files 3 --json --quiet | jq -e '.recommended_level'` prints the number.\n- [ ] T017 Check the error paths (no file). Verify: `bash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --loc` exits 1 and prints `ERROR: --loc requires a numeric value` on stderr; `bash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet` exits 1 and prints `At least --loc or --files must be provided`; `bash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --bogus` exits 1 and prints `ERROR: Unknown option: --bogus`.\n- [ ] T018 Check the help text (no file). Verify: `bash \"$SCRIPT\" --help` exits 0, lists `--quiet` in OPTIONS, and shows an example that uses it; the header OPTIONS block lists the same option.\n- [ ] T019 Run the focused regression test (no file). Verify: `cd \"$S\" && npx vitest run runtime/cli/tests/recommend-level-quiet.vitest.ts --config vitest.config.ts` prints `Test Files 1 passed`.\n- [ ] T020 Run the full CLI suite (no file). Verify: `cd \"$S\" && npm run test --workspace=@spec-kit/cli` exits 0, and `runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.js` still passes.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-4 -->\n## Phase 4: Documentation and Close\n\n- [ ] T021 Synchronize this packet with what shipped (`spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`). Record any deviation from the plan in this file rather than silently correcting it.\n- [ ] T022 Remove the scratch captures after T015 has been read and its result recorded (`scratch/baseline/`).\n- [ ] T023 Mark each acceptance criterion in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its observed evidence (`acceptance-criteria.md`).\n- [ ] T024 Run strict validation on the packet (no file). Verify: `bash \"$S/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh\" \"$P\" --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-4 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md (REQ-001 through REQ-007)\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md (section 3 and ADR-001)\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available (bash 3.2, the vitest CLI project)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n` passes on the modified script\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No new stderr output appears on any success path\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error handling unchanged: every existing error keeps its message and exit code\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] Code follows the file's patterns (`output_*` functions, `QUIET_OUTPUT` beside `JSON_OUTPUT`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Manual matrix run: text, quiet, json and json + quiet, each with and without `--no-recommend-phases`\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested: `--help` with `--quiet`, repeated `--quiet`, missing value, no inputs\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated: exit 1 and the stderr message preserved\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Every output path is inventoried: `output_text`, `output_json`, `output_quiet`\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed with `rg -n 'output_(text|json|quiet)|Recommended Level:' \"$SCRIPT\"`\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory complete